---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';

const updated = '7 November 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use | Qivy"
  description="Terms for using qivy.in: how the content may be used, the limits of technical guidance, and what is and is not warranted."
>
  <section class="hdr wrap">
    <Breadcrumbs crumbs={[{ label: 'Terms' }]} />
    <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
    <p class="meta">Last updated {updated}</p>
  </section>

  <div class="wrap body">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        Qivy publishes technical guidance for free. Read it, use it, check it
        before you rely on it for anything that matters, and don't republish it
        wholesale as your own.
      </p>

      <h2>Using the content</h2>
      <p>
        You are welcome to read, apply and share Qivy's articles, and to quote
        from them with attribution and a link. Code and configuration snippets
        in articles may be used freely in your own projects.
      </p>
      <p>
        Please don't republish whole articles — on a website, in a newsletter,
        or as AI-generated derivatives presented as original work. A link costs
        you nothing and keeps the original findable.
      </p>

      <h2>Accuracy and the limits of this guidance</h2>
      <p>
        Articles are written to be correct at the time of publication, and
        every article shows whether it was <strong>Tested</strong> (actually
        run) or <strong>Researched</strong> (verified against documentation but
        not personally run), with its sources listed.
      </p>
      <p>
        Technology moves. Interfaces are redesigned, flags are renamed, APIs
        break, pricing changes and free tiers disappear. An article that was
        accurate when written can be wrong months later. <strong>Check the
        publication date and the vendor's current documentation before relying
        on anything here.</strong>
      </p>
      <p>
        This matters most for anything involving your data or your money.
        Automation scripts can delete files, overwrite spreadsheets and send
        messages you didn't intend. Test on sample data first. Pricing shown
        for any tool carries the date it was checked and is a starting point,
        not a quote.
      </p>

      <h2>No warranty</h2>
      <p>
        The content is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. Qivy
        does not guarantee that any instruction, script or configuration will
        work in your environment, and accepts no liability for data loss,
        service costs, downtime or other damage arising from following it. You
        remain responsible for what you run on your own systems.
      </p>

      <h2>Third-party tools and links</h2>
      <p>
        Qivy writes about software it does not control. Links to tools,
        documentation and vendors are provided for reference and are not
        endorsements, and Qivy is not responsible for those services, their
        terms, their pricing or their continued existence.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nothing on this site is a paid placement. No vendor pays to be included
        in an article or in the Tools list.
      </p>

      <h2>Availability</h2>
      <p>
        Qivy is a personal publication offered free of charge. There is no
        uptime commitment, and articles may be updated, corrected, archived or
        removed at any time.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        These terms may be updated; the date above reflects the latest version,
        and the change history is public in the site's
        <a href="https://github.com/fshbet/qivy-site" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">repository</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions, or a correction to report:
        <a href="https://github.com/fshbet" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">github.com/fshbet</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hdr {
    padding-block: var(--sp-6);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--bd);
  }
  h1 {
    margin-top: var(--sp-5);
    font-size: var(--fs-3xl);
  }
  .meta {
    margin-top: var(--sp-3);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-xs);
    color: var(--text-3);
  }
  .body {
    padding-top: var(--sp-7);
  }
</style>
